Why copyleft: the SVG curve tracing is performed by potrace, which is GPL-2.0.

  * scripts/native/trace_core.dll
        compiles potrace 1.16 (https://potrace.sourceforge.net/) behind a thin
        C ABI wrapper (scripts/native/trace_core.cpp). Its full license text is
        scripts/native/COPYING.
  * potracer (pip package, GPLv2+)
        the pure-Python fallback used when the DLL is absent or disabled.

Everything else in this directory is original work and is released under the same
license for consistency:

  * scripts/build_svg.py, vectorize.py, seal_gaps.py, metric.py, steps.py,
    autotune.py, render.py, render.js, smooth_svg.py, native_loader.py,
    paint_process.py
  * tests/, IMPLEMENTATION.md, SKILL.md

The palette quantizer (scripts/native/palette_core.cpp) is original code with no
potrace dependency; it is licensed under the same GPL-2.0-or-later terms to keep
the directory single-licensed.

Corresponding source: the potrace 1.16 sources needed to rebuild trace_core.dll
are available from the upstream address above; build steps are in
scripts/native/README.md.

vtracer (scripts/smooth_svg.py) is MIT-licensed and is NOT part of the GPL-bound
tracing path; it is an optional alternative renderer.
